; ladder.eval — the progression ladder, in Michael's protocol.
;
;   a room with a corridor coming off it
;   the party at the FAR END of the corridor
;   monster(s) in the middle of the room
;   the party WALKS in and engages
;   the battle is recorded
;   then tp away, summon the next, repeat
;
; TWO THINGS MAKE THIS A LADDER RATHER THAN A LIST OF FIGHTS.
;
; NO HEALING BETWEEN RUNGS. This measures ATTRITION — how the party arrives at
; the next fight is the entire question — so nothing here restores anything.
; Whatever regen happens during the walk in is the only recovery there is, and
; today that is stamina and mana but NOT health (docs/health-and-healing.md).
; Watch `taken` accumulate down the file: that is the ladder working.
;
; THE ESCALATION IS COUNT FIRST, THEN STRENGTH. Three of the same weak monster
; one after another, then two at once, then three, then four — and only then a
; tougher type. Difficulty is not one axis, and a party that handles four weak
; monsters is not the same as one that handles a single strong one.
;
; The arena is rebuilt for every rung, which IS the "tp away": it clears the
; previous monsters and returns the party to the corridor end. It does not touch
; their health, which is the point.
;
; Geometry (7x7 room, 6-cell corridor, map 28x24):
;   room centre  14,12   <- monsters
;   corridor end 14,21   <- the party starts here, facing NORTH to walk in
; The `arena` line prints what it actually carved; check it against those.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 31
autoattack on

; ============ TIER 1: one skel_swarm, three times over ====================
; The same trivial encounter repeatedly. If the party cannot clear three of
; these without recovery, nothing further up the ladder means anything.

arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 1.1: 1x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 1.2: 1x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 1.3: 1x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

; ============ TIER 2: the same monster, two at once ========================
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 13 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 2: 2x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

; ============ TIER 3: three at once ========================================
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 13 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 15 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 3: 3x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

; ============ TIER 4: four at once =========================================
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_swarm 14 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 13 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 15 12 south
spawn skel_swarm 14 11 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 4: 4x skel_swarm ===
party
tally

; ============ TIER 5: a tougher TYPE, back to one ==========================
; The other axis. A skeleton is 16 hp against the swarm's 6.
arena room 7 6
spawn skeleton 14 12 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 5: 1x skeleton ===
party
tally

; ============ TIER 6: the same type, SCALED ================================
; The second axis Michael asked for: a strength multiplier sweeps difficulty
; BETWEEN authored types. A result here points at where a monster is missing
; rather than at one to retune.
arena room 7 6
spawn skeleton 14 12 south 2.0
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 6: 1x skeleton x2.0 ===
party
tally
monsters
state
